    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d506">

                <pb facs="0584" n="254 [524]" xml:id="pg524"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Baron Saurma</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-04-22"><hi rendition="#italic">April 22,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 48.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Referring to this Department’s note
                    of the 5th ultimo, in relation to the participation of this Government in the
                    ceremonies attending the opening of the Northern Baltic Canal in June next, I
                    have the honor to apprise you of the receipt of a letter of the 18th instant
                    from the Secretary of the Navy; in which he states that in addition to the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">San Francisco</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Marblehead</hi>, the U. S. ships <hi rendition="#italic">New York</hi> and
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Columbia</hi> will proceed to Kiel with the
                    squadron, under the command of Rear-Admiral W. A. Kirkland. The <hi
                        rendition="#italic">New York</hi> will be under the command of Capt. R. D.
                    Evans, and the <hi rendition="#italic">Columbia</hi> of Capt. G. W. Sumner.</p>
                <p>Rear-Admiral Kirkland has been instructed to place himself, early in June, in
                    communication with the German Government, through the United States ambassador
                    at Berlin, with a view to his communicating directly with the German admiral in
                    command of the combined fleet and the naval review.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
